&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Snorkel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Snorkel, we believe meaningful AI doesn’t start with the model, it starts with the data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re on a mission to help enterprises transform expert knowledge into specialized AI at scale. The AI landscape has gone through incredible changes since 2015, when Snorkel started as a research project in the Stanford AI Lab, to the generative AI breakthroughs of today. But one thing has remained constant: the data you use to build AI is the key to achieving differentiation, high performance, and production-ready systems. We work with some of the world’s largest organizations to empower scientists, engineers, financial experts, product creators, journalists, and more to build custom AI with their data faster than ever before. Excited to help us redefine how AI is built? Apply to be the newest Snorkeler!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Snorkel AI is looking for a Head of Technical Recruiting to build and lead the technical recruiting engine that will support our next stage of growth. This leader will own the strategy, team, operating model, and execution required to hire exceptional talent across Engineering, Research, Product, Forward Deployed Engineering, and Applied AI Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact leadership role for someone who has built and scaled technical recruiting teams in hyper-growth startup environments, ideally from roughly 100 to 1,000 employees. We are looking for a builder: someone who knows how to design a recruiting function from the ground up, develop a high-performing team, partner deeply with technical leaders, and compete creatively for scarce talent in one of the most competitive markets in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has operated in the Bay Area technical talent market, understands the pace and ambiguity of high-growth startups, and brings strong instincts for hiring in AI, infrastructure, data, machine learning, developer tools, or other deeply technical domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and scale Snorkel AI’s technical recruiting function across Engineering, Research, Product, FDE, and Applied AI Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, develop, and manage a high-performing team of technical recruiters, sourcers, and recruiting leaders as the company scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the overall technical recruiting strategy, including workforce planning, pipeline development, sourcing strategy, candidate experience, closing strategy, and capacity planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Engineering, Research, Product, and other technical leaders to understand business priorities and translate them into actionable hiring plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a world-class recruiting operating model that balances speed, quality, rigor, and an exceptional candidate experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop creative sourcing strategies for highly competitive technical and AI talent markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to identify bottlenecks, improve conversion, forecast hiring outcomes, and drive accountability across the recruiting process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and track key technical recruiting metrics, including pipeline health, pass-through rates, time to fill, offer acceptance, source effectiveness, candidate experience, and quality of hire indicators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach hiring managers and interview teams on effective assessment, structured interviewing, calibration, and closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable processes while remaining hands-on and close to the work where needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Snorkel AI externally as an employer of choice for world-class technical talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and leading technical recruiting teams in a hyper-growth startup environment, ideally at a company scaling from approximately 100 to 1,000 employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience recruiting for technical functions such as Engineering, Research, Product, Machine Learning, AI, Infrastructure, Data, Applied AI, or similar areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of the Bay Area technical talent market and competitive AI/startup hiring landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building recruiting teams, developing recruiters, and creating scalable recruiting practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering directly with senior technical and business leaders on hiring strategy, prioritization, tradeoffs, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data orientation, with the ability to use recruiting metrics to diagnose problems, drive decisions, and communicate progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated creativity in sourcing, pipeline generation, talent mapping, and candidate engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to influence across technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in ambiguity and building systems, processes, and teams where they may not yet exist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high bar for talent, candidate experience, and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Locations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;San Francisco or New York - Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation range is $170,000 - $300,000. All offers also include equity in the form of employee stock options. Our compensation ranges are determined by role, level, and location. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI - SM1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation will be determined based on factors including skills, qualifications, experience, and geographic location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary range(s) for this role&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$170,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$300,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be Your Best at Snorkel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Snorkel AI means becoming part of a company that has market proven solutions, robust funding, and is scaling rapidly—offering a unique combination of stability and the excitement of high growth. As a member of our team, you’ll have meaningful opportunities to shape priorities and initiatives, influence key strategic decisions, and directly impact our ongoing success. Whether you’re looking to deepen your technical expertise, explore leadership opportunities, or learn new skills across multiple functions, you’re fully supported in building your career in an environment designed for growth, learning, and shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Snorkel AI is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer and is committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. Snorkel AI embraces diversity and provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment. Snorkel AI prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type on the basis of race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. All employment is decided on the basis of qualifications, performance, merit, and business need.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment. Please contact us to request accommodation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Snorkel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Snorkel, we believe meaningful AI doesn’t start with the model, it starts with the data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re on a mission to help enterprises transform expert knowledge into specialized AI at scale. The AI landscape has gone through incredible changes since 2015, when Snorkel started as a research project in the Stanford AI Lab, to the generative AI breakthroughs of today. But one thing has remained constant: the data you use to build AI is the key to achieving differentiation, high performance, and production-ready systems. We work with some of the world’s largest organizations to empower scientists, engineers, financial experts, product creators, journalists, and more to build custom AI with their data faster than ever before. Excited to help us redefine how AI is built? Apply to be the newest Snorkeler!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Job Description&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;IT Platform &amp;amp; Automation Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; who treats internal infrastructure like a product—not a firefighting exercise. This is not a traditional helpdesk or &quot;break-fix&quot; role. You&#39;ll be the architect behind our internal employee experience, acting as the connective tissue between our office network, collaboration services, security stack, and core business systems (People Tech, CRM, and Engineering tools).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you prefer writing Python scripts over manually resetting passwords, and if you get excited about connecting Claude AI to Greenhouse via custom Slack workflows, we want to talk to you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is NOT:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A traditional helpdesk position.&lt;/strong&gt; You won&#39;t be resetting passwords or shipping laptops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A pure networking role.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll touch networks, but automation is the priority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A machine learning engineer role.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll experiment with AI, but you won&#39;t build vector databases or train models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;What You will Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity, Endpoint &amp;amp; Network (The Foundation)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity &amp;amp; Access Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Own our IdP (Okta/Auth0). Implement and automate SSO, MFA enforcement, and SCIM provisioning across all SaaS tools. Enforce zero-trust principles everywhere.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Endpoint Lifecycle:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the full hardware and MDM lifecycle. Automate device provisioning, configuration, and secure deployment using Jamf and Intune. Build zero-touch onboarding workflows. &lt;em&gt;(Note: You will own the automation and security profiles; physical device shipping/fulfillment is handled by our IT Ops coordinators.)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network Engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, deploy, and maintain high-availability office networking (cloud-managed switching/routing, Wi-Fi) and secure remote access solutions (ZTNA/VPN) for a hybrid workforce. We prioritize automation-first engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom Integrations &amp;amp; Automation (The Builder Work)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;API Integrations:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect and build custom integrations between our core SaaS stack—syncing data between Okta, Greenhouse, Notion, and our CRM to eliminate manual data entry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workflow Orchestration:&lt;/strong&gt; Own our internal automation layer. We currently use a mix of lightweight no-code tools (Zapier, App Script, AppSheet) and custom Python. We&#39;re actively phasing out low-code for mission-critical paths—you&#39;ll have permission to replace them with proper code. To be clear: this is a coding-heavy role. You&#39;ll spend the majority of your time writing code, not clicking in UIs. The no-code tools are placeholders—we expect you to replace or maintain them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal Tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain internal dashboards and Slack apps that give employees self-service access to IT, HR, and facilities requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; LLM Experimentation (The Innovation Work)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Integrations:&lt;/strong&gt; Review and assess connectors (MCP) if available. Otherwise, build lightweight API wrappers and prompt engineering pipelines to connect LLMs (Claude, OpenAI) to internal tools like Slack and Notion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R&amp;amp;D Time:&lt;/strong&gt; Dedicated time each sprint to experiment with new AI models and identify productivity gains for the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Automation &amp;amp; Compliance (The Glue)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Scripting:&lt;/strong&gt; Write robust scripts (Python, Bash, PowerShell) to automate security monitoring, endpoint patch management, and compliance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alert Correlation:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect centralized alerting pipelines by integrating EDR/SIEM webhooks into Slack via native integrations (CrowdStrike), filtering noise and surfacing only actionable security anomalies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance Automation:&lt;/strong&gt; Create automated audit trails, access reviews, and reporting to support SOC2 / ISO compliance efforts—no more manual spreadsheet work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech Stack Summary:&lt;/strong&gt; Python, Okta/Azure AD, Jamf/Intune, Slack API, Greenhouse API, Notion API, Claude/OpenAI APIs, CrowdStrike, Meraki/cloud-networking, Google Workspace + GAM, Jira.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Foundation (Must-Have Baseline)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 4+ years in IT Engineering, Systems Engineering, or Platform roles with a heavy emphasis on automation and APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coding Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced Python or JavaScript/Node.js. You treat your scripts like software—git, CI/CD, testing, and documentation are non-negotiable. Our current automation stack is built on Python. Familiarity with either is sufficient—we don&#39;t expect you to know both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;API Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience building custom integrations using REST/GraphQL APIs. You know how to read documentation, handle OAuth2, and parse JSON in your sleep.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IdP &amp;amp; MDM Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with Okta or Azure AD (SCIM, Workflows, automation) AND at least one MDM solution (Jamf and Intune).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security-First Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; You understand least privilege, automated patching, and think about security in every integration you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary Focus Areas (Where You&#39;ll Spend Most of Your Time)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core:&lt;/strong&gt; Identity &amp;amp; Workflow Automation (Okta, SCIM, custom scripting)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core:&lt;/strong&gt; Endpoint Management &amp;amp; security ops related&amp;nbsp; (MDM, zero-touch deployment, patching)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secondary:&lt;/strong&gt; Networking (TCP/IP, VLANs, Wi-Fi, VPN/ZTNA—enough to troubleshoot and configure, not necessarily design from scratch)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We prioritize automation-first engineers who can learn networking depth on the job. If you&#39;re a networking rockstar who&#39;s also strong on MDM and automation, even better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High-Value Differentiators (Stand Out From the Crowd)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with Okta, People Tech (Rippling and Greenhouse), Notion, or Slack APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building with LLM APIs (Anthropic Claude, OpenAI) for internal tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Infrastructure as Code (Terraform)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing IT systems for SOC2 or ISO 27001 audits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Google Workspace administration and GAM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with zero-touch deployment workflows (Apple Business Manager, Windows Autopilot)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation will be determined based on factors including skills, qualifications, experience, and geographic location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary range(s) for this role&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$120,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$185,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be Your Best at Snorkel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Snorkel AI means becoming part of a company that has market proven solutions, robust funding, and is scaling rapidly—offering a unique combination of stability and the excitement of high growth. As a member of our team, you’ll have meaningful opportunities to shape priorities and initiatives, influence key strategic decisions, and directly impact our ongoing success. Whether you’re looking to deepen your technical expertise, explore leadership opportunities, or learn new skills across multiple functions, you’re fully supported in building your career in an environment designed for growth, learning, and shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
