&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for talented and versatile Product Engineers to join our team. In this role, you&#39;ll build end-to-end products — from front-end interfaces through the APIs and services that power them — that make sophisticated workflows simple for our users. You&#39;ll work closely with product, design, and engineering teams to translate complex requirements into elegant, high-quality experiences, moving fluidly across the stack to get the job done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for talented Engineers who bring strong technical depth in React and TypeScript (and are comfortable working further down the stack when needed), a sharp product sense, and a passion for building software that makes sophisticated workflows feel intuitive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, ship, and maintain high-quality product features with full ownership from design through production, working across the front end and, as needed, the services that support it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable operations teams to move fast by building the right abstractions and tools that provide safe use of agent workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with designers, product managers, and engineers to define and implement solutions that push the product forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to architecture decisions across the stack — advocating for scalability, maintainability, and clean code principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive best practices for accessibility, responsiveness, and cross-browser compatibility within your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build APIs and services where a feature calls for it, ensuring a clean contract between front end and back end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in and contribute to code reviews, raising the quality bar across the codebase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify technical challenges and propose solutions to improve the product engineering ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve performance and production issues across the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work a hybrid schedule with at least three days per week in San Francisco, CA office or in our New York City office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring for Product Engineers at several levels, but the core experience is below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of professional experience in software engineering, with strong depth in React and TypeScript and solid full-stack or front-end fundamentals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of HTML5, CSS3, and modern CSS frameworks (e.g., Tailwind)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with state management libraries (e.g., Redux, React Context API)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort designing and consuming RESTful APIs, and enough back-end fluency (Node.js, Python, or similar) to build or extend a service when a feature requires it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with responsive design, adaptive design, and accessibility standards (WCAG)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record delivering high-quality, scalable, and maintainable code in a product environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills — able to articulate technical decisions clearly to cross-functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prototype and iterate quickly on sophisticated user workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working independently and making scoped technical decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating in an agile, cross-functional team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with design systems and building reusable component libraries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with server-side rendering frameworks (e.g., Next.js)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with performance optimization for web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work in developer tools or data-heavy product environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a feature across the full stack, from database or service layer through UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have meaningful ownership over a product used by technical and enterprise teams solving real, high-stakes problems. This isn&#39;t a feature-factory role — you&#39;ll be working on interfaces and the systems behind them to make genuinely complex workflows feel simple, with a team that cares deeply about craft.&lt;/p&gt;
